1
00:05:15,652 --> 00:05:21,652
Oceans rise. Cities fall. Hope survives.

2
00:10:31,304 --> 00:10:37,304
Deep Impact is a action, drama, science fiction film directed by Mimi Leder.

3
00:15:46,956 --> 00:15:52,956
A seven-mile-wide space rock is hurtling toward Earth,
threatening to obliterate the planet.

4
00:21:02,608 --> 00:21:08,608
Now, it's up to the president of the United States to save the world.

5
00:26:18,260 --> 00:26:24,260
He appoints a tough-as-nails veteran astronaut to lead a joint
American-Russian crew into space to destroy the comet before impact.

6
00:31:33,913 --> 00:31:39,913
Meanwhile, an enterprising reporter uses her smarts
to uncover the scoop of the century.

7
00:36:49,565 --> 00:36:55,565
Capt. Spurgeon 'Fish' Tanner, played by Robert Duvall.

8
00:42:05,217 --> 00:42:11,217
Jenny Lerner, played by Téa Leoni.

9
00:47:20,869 --> 00:47:26,869
Leo Biederman, played by Elijah Wood.

10
00:52:36,521 --> 00:52:42,521
Robin Lerner, played by Vanessa Redgrave.

11
00:57:52,173 --> 00:57:58,173
President Tom Beck, played by Morgan Freeman.

12
01:03:07,826 --> 01:03:13,826
Jason Lerner, played by Maximilian Schell.

13
01:08:23,478 --> 01:08:29,478
Deep Impact is a 1998 American science fiction disaster film directed by Mimi Leder, written by Bruce Joel Rubin and Michael
Tolkin, and starring Robert Duvall, Téa Leoni, Elijah Wood, Vanessa Redgrave, Maximilian Schell, and Morgan Freeman.

14
01:13:39,130 --> 01:13:45,130
Steven Spielberg served as an executive producer of this film.

15
01:18:54,782 --> 01:19:00,782
It was released by Paramount Pictures in North America and by
DreamWorks Pictures internationally on May 8, 1998.

16
01:24:10,434 --> 01:24:16,434
The film depicts humanity's attempts to prepare for and destroy a 7-mile (11 km)
wide comet set to collide with Earth and cause a mass extinction.

17
01:29:26,086 --> 01:29:32,086
Deep Impact was released in the same summer as the similarly themed Armageddon, which fared better
at the box office, while astronomers described Deep Impact as being more accurate.

18
01:34:41,739 --> 01:34:47,739
Deep Impact was slightly better received critically than
Armageddon, although both ultimately received mixed reviews.

19
01:39:57,391 --> 01:40:03,391
Deep Impact grossed over $349.5 million worldwide on an $80 million
production budget, becoming the sixth highest-grossing film of 1998.

20
01:45:13,043 --> 01:45:19,043
It was the final film by cinematographer Dietrich
Lohmann, who died before the film's release.

21
01:50:28,695 --> 01:50:34,695
The film explores themes of usa president, nasa,
natural disaster, space mission, comet.

22
01:55:44,347 --> 01:55:50,347
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
